# Skill Router

Unlike the other `.mdc` rules in this repo (which apply only when their
own description matches the request), this one is `alwaysApply: true` —
Cursor loads it for every request in this project.

Before doing any non-trivial task:

1. Read `skills/manifest.json` (regenerate it first if it looks stale:
   `python3 skills/skill-router/scripts/build_manifest.py`).
2. If an installed skill's description matches the task, read its full
   `SKILL.md` and follow it — no need to ask which skill to use.
3. If nothing installed matches, read
   `skills/skill-router/SKILL.md` in full — it covers searching for a
   pre-made skill, converting one of the user's own MCP repos, or
   building a new one from scratch, then installing it into this repo
   (commit, push, sync the Cursor clone + symlink) — all pre-approved,
   standing procedure, not something to ask permission for step by step.
4. The one thing to flag rather than do silently: anything needing a new
   credential/API key, or adopting a stranger's code with a real
   licensing/safety concern.
